fields.value:
{{Draftnotes
| name = Shadow Poison
| desc = Has {{M|Autocast}} on if there are enemies affected by {{Symbol|Modifier|Debuff}} {{Code|shadow_demon_shadow_poison}}.<br><br>Toggle off acts as {{A|Shadow Demon|Shadow Poison Release}} and procs the {{M|magical}} {{M|spell damage}} instance.
}}

 * The ability has two main components:
** [[File:Dota2 Condition-1.png|21px|1]] {{Symbol|Projectile|Base}}
*** {{Symbol|Projectile|Travel}}
**** Has a {{#var:Shadow Poison basic1}}-{{M|projectile speed}}, reaching max distance in {{#expr:{{#var:Shadow Poison value1}}/{{#var:Shadow Poison basic1}}}} seconds. 
**** {{Symbol|Vision|Flying}}
***** Grants a non-lingering 350-radius [[flying vision]] centered around the [[projectile]] as it travels.
***** Grants a 3.5-second 300-radius flying vision upon reaching the max distance.
**** {{Symbol|Target|AreaAlt}} {{to}} {{Symbol|Affect|Enemy}} {{Symbol|Modifier|Debuff}} {{Code|shadow_demon_shadow_poison}}
***** The ability effects are applied as follows within the projectile's radius per affected enemy unit:
*****# Grants a 3.5-second 300-radius flying vision over the affected unit.
*****# Adds 1 debuff stack.
*****# The base {{M|magical}} {{M|spell damage}}.
***** From the same source:
****** Reapplying the debuff update the ability values and refreshes the stack duration.
***** From different sources:
****** Reapplying the debuff increases the stack count of the first applied stack and does not update the ability values.
*** {{Symbol|Affect|Enemy}}
**** Affects the following units:
***** {{M|Invisible}} units.
**** Does not affect the following units:
***** {{M|Hidden}} units of other sources, except {{A|Shadow Demon|Disruption}}.
***** {{M|Invulnerable}} units.
** [[File:Dota2 Condition-2.png|21px|2]] {{Symbol|Spell Damage}}
*** The spell damage component has no stack limit.
*** Procs the final spell damage in the following conditions:
**** Upon {{A|Shadow Demon|Shadow Poison Release}} cast.
**** Upon losing the {{Symbol|Modifier|Debuff}} {{Code|shadow_demon_shadow_poison}} in any way.
*** The final spell damage has two ability formulas:
**** {{Code|When 1 ≤ Stack ≤ 5}}
***** {{cf|expr}} {{Code|MultipliedDmg × ({{#var:Shadow Poison type1 value2}}^( Stack - 1 ))}}
***** Hence with {{#var:Shadow Poison type1 value1}} stacks, the ability can optimally deal up to {{calc|v1*{{#var:Shadow Poison type1 value2}}^({{#var:Shadow Poison type1 value1}}-1)|v1={{#var:Shadow Poison type1 value4}}}} ({{Symbol|bonus t1r}} {{ValueColor||{{calc|(v1*{{#var:Shadow Poison type1 value2}}^({{#var:Shadow Poison type1 value1}}-1))*(1+{{Show|T|Shadow Demon|v1r}}/100)|v1={{#var:Shadow Poison type1 value4}}}}|10tal}}) {{M|magical}} {{M|spell damage}} ([[before reductions]]).
**** {{Code|When Stack ≥ 6}}
***** {{cf|expr}} {{Code|( 16 × MultipliedDmg ) + IncrementDmg × ( Stack - 5 )}}

 {{Gamedesc
| image = {{#var:Shadow Poison icon0}}
| desc = Deals damage in a line, and afflicts enemy units with a poison effect. The poison deals 1/2/4/8/16 times the stack damage based on the number of stacks on the target, up to 5 stacks. Additional stacks cause 60 damage each.  This deferred damage is dealt when Shadow Poison's duration is expired, or the Release sub-ability is used.
}}
* {{Symbol|Modifier|Stack}} {{Symbol|fx|v}}
** The number of stack value indicator is capped visually at 19 and is visible ally-only.

